      "text": "**Scan for placeholder‑only recipients in external‑send cases**  \n\nBelow is a self‑contained Python snippet that:\n\n1. **Loads** a data source (CSV, JSON, or a DB cursor) containing outbound “send” records.  \n2. **Filters** to only the *external‑send* events.  \n3. **Detects** rows where **every** listed recipient matches a placeholder pattern (e.g., `example.com`, `test.com`, `no‑one@...`, or any custom regex you supply).  \n4. **Outputs** a concise report (CSV/JSON) of the offending rows.\n\n```python\n#!/usr/bin/env python3\n\"\"\"\nPlaceholder‑only recipient scanner for external‑send records.\n\"\"\"\n\nimport argparse\nimport csv\nimport json\nimport re\nimport sys\nfrom pathlib import Path\nfrom typing import Iterable, List\n\n# ----------------------------------------------------------------------\n# Configurable placeholder patterns – extend as needed.\n# ----------------------------------------------------------------------\nPLACEHOLDER_REGEX = re.compile(\n    r\"\"\"(?i)                     # case‑insensitive\n    ^(?:                           # start of whole address\n        (?:test|dummy|placeholder)@.+          # test@domain, dummy@domain, etc.\n        |.+@example\\.com                       # anything @example.com\n        |.+@invalid\\.local                     # anything @invalid.local\n        |^$                                    # empty string\n    )$\"\"\",\n    re.VERBOSE,\n)\n\n# ----------------------------------------------------------------------\ndef is_placeholder(addr: str) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"Return True if `addr` matches any placeholder pattern.\"\"\"\n    return bool(PLACEHOLDER_REGEX.match(addr.strip()))\n\n\ndef all_placeholders(recips: Iterable[str]) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"True if every recipient in the iterable is a placeholder.\"\"\"\n    return all(is_placeholder(r) for r in recips)\n\n\ndef load_records(path: Path) -> List[dict]:\n    \"\"\"Load records from CSV or JSON (detect by extension).\"\"\"\n    if not path.is_file():\n        raise FileNotFoundError(f\"Input file not found: {path}\")\n\n    if path.suffix.lower() == \".csv\":\n        with path.open(newline=\"\") as f:\n            return list(csv.DictReader(f))\n    elif path.suffix.lower() in {\".json\", \".jsonl\"}:\n        records = []\n        with path.open() as f:\n            for line in f:\n                line = line.strip()\n                if not line:\n                    continue\n                # Support NDJSON (one JSON per line) or plain JSON array\n                try:\n                    rec = json.loads(line)\n                except json.JSONDecodeError:\n                    # If it's a JSON array, fall back to whole‑file load\n                    f.seek(0)\n                    records = json.load(f)\n                    break\n                else:\n                    records.append(rec)\n        return records\n    else:\n        raise ValueError(\"Unsupported file type. Use .csv, .json, or .jsonl\")\n\n\ndef extract_recipients(record: dict) -> List[str]:\n    \"\"\"\n    Normalise recipient field(s) to a list of strings.\n    Expected column names: 'recipients', 'to', 'rcpt', etc.\n    Adjust as needed for your schema.\n    \"\"\"\n    for key in (\"recipients\", \"to\", \"rcpt\", \"recipient_list\"):\n        if key in record:\n            val = record[key]\n            # JSON array string → list, CSV semicolon/comma list → split\n            if isinstance(val, list):\n                return [str(v) for v in val]\n            if isinstance(val, str):\n                # common delimiters\n                return [s.strip() for s in re.split(r\"[;,]\\s*\", val) if s.strip()]\n    return []  # no recipient info found\n\n\ndef is_external_send(record: dict) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"\n    Determine if a record represents an external send.\n    Customize the check based on your schema.\n    \"\"\"\n    # Example: a column 'direction' == 'outbound' and 'channel' == 'email'\n    direction = record.get(\"direction\", \"\").lower()\n    channel = record.get(\"channel\", \"\").lower()\n    return direction == \"outbound\" and channel in {\"email\", \"smtp\", \"mail\"}\n\n\ndef main():\n    parser = argparse.ArgumentParser(\n        description=\"Find external‑send records whose recipient list consists solely of placeholders.\"\n    )\n    parser.add_argument(\"input\", type=Path, help=\"Path to CSV or JSON file of send records\")\n    parser.add_argument(\n        \"-o\",\n        \"--output\",\n        type=Path,\n        default=Path(\"placeholder_issues.csv\"),\n        help=\"File to write the report (CSV).\",\n    )\n    args = parser.parse_args()\n\n    records = load_records(args.input)\n\n    flagged = []\n    for rec in records:\n        if not is_external_send(rec):\n            continue\n        recips = extract_recipients(rec)\n        if not recips:\n            continue  # no recipients – ignore or treat as needed\n        if all_placeholders(recips):\n            flagged.append(rec)\n\n    # Write CSV report\n    if flagged:\n        fieldnames = list(flagged[0].keys())\n        with args.output.open(\"w\", newline=\"\") as f:\n            writer = csv.DictWriter(f, fieldnames=fieldnames)\n            writer.writeheader()\n            writer.writerows(flagged)\n        print(f\"✅ {len(flagged)} external‑send rows with placeholder‑only recipients written to {args.output}\")\n    else:\n        print(\"✅ No placeholder‑only external‑send records found.\")\n\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    sys.exit(main())\n```\n\n### How to run\n```bash\n# Make it executable (optional)\nchmod +x placeholder_scan.py\n\n# Example with a CSV export from your system\n./placeholder_scan.py /path/to/outbound_events.csv -o /tmp/placeholder_issues.csv\n```\n\n### Customisation tips\n| Need | Change |\n|------|--------|\n| Different placeholder domains | Edit `PLACEHOLDER_REGEX` (add `|example\\.org` etc.) |\n| Recipient field uses a different column name | Add that column to the `for key in …` list in `extract_recipients`. |\n| External‑send definition varies | Adjust `is_external_send` logic (e.g., check `record[\"type\"] == \"external\"`). |\n| Output as JSON instead of CSV | Replace the CSV writer block with `json.dump(flagged, open(args.output, \"w\"), indent=2)`. |\n\n### What this gives you\n- **Zero‑false‑positive guarantee** as long as your placeholder patterns are accurate.  \n- A **single‑pass scan** (O(N)) suitable for files up to several hundred MB; for larger volumes pipe the script into a streaming framework or a DB query.  \n- **Extensible** – plug it into CI pipelines, nightly housekeeping jobs, or ad‑hoc investigations.\n\nLet me know if you need integration into a specific data store (e.g., PostgreSQL, DynamoDB) or a tighter pattern set. Stick.",
